1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,533
In this video you will install a game over the network: from a browser, with an FTP

2
00:00:05,533 --> 00:00:07,867
program, or from an Ownfoil server.

3
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:11,600
You will also open the console's files on a PC or phone.

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,600
The console and the PC or phone must be on the same network.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,533
The top of the screen shows the network name and the console's IP address.

6
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:23,800
If it says "No Internet", connect to Wi-Fi first.

7
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:28,133
A guest Wi-Fi usually isolates devices, so use your home network.

8
00:00:28,133 --> 00:00:32,133
And start Kefir Hub in Title Mode, as in the previous video.

9
00:00:32,133 --> 00:00:37,467
Important: the web page has no password, and FTP lets anyone in with the default

10
00:00:37,467 --> 00:00:39,467
settings.

11
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:45,000
While a server runs, anyone on the same network can read, download and delete files

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
on the microSD card.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,133
So use these servers only at home, and stop the web server when you are done.

14
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:54,133
Let's start with the browser.

15
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:57,467
On the Tools tab press plus and choose Web Server.

16
00:00:57,467 --> 00:01:02,600
If Kefir Hub was started from the Album, the panel "Web Server — Applet Mode"

17
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,600
appears first.

18
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,533
Choose "Start anyway", or install the Title Mode forwarder.

19
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:12,933
The Web Sharing Server window opens with a QR code and an address.

20
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:18,067
Scan the code with your phone, or type the address into a browser on your PC.

21
00:01:18,067 --> 00:01:23,467
If the kefir.local address does not open, type the IP address from the top of the

22
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:25,467
console screen instead.

23
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:28,000
If the address had a port, add it too.

24
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,067
The Kefir Hub Files page opens.

25
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:32,067
It is in English only.

26
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:35,000
Click Add to Upload and pick the game files.

27
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Then click Queue.

28
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,200
Game files already have Install directly ticked.

29
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,200
Click Start transfers.

30
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:47,067
The game installs while it uploads, and the file is not kept on the card.

31
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:51,933
The console shows "Web install" with a percentage and the time remaining.

32
00:01:51,933 --> 00:01:55,800
When the game is installed you see "Web install success!".

33
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:01,333
If you untick Install directly, the game file is only saved into the folder open in

34
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:03,333
the browser.

35
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:06,667
The same page shows the files on the microSD card.

36
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:09,267
Click a file to download it to your PC.

37
00:02:09,267 --> 00:02:13,400
Select several and click Download Selected or Delete Selected.

38
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:16,600
Download a very large file by clicking its name.

39
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:21,933
Download Selected keeps the whole file in the browser's memory until it is done.

40
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:27,400
The Screenshots button opens the console's album: screenshots and videos with game

41
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,400
names.

42
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,867
Click a screenshot to open it full size and save it.

43
00:02:32,867 --> 00:02:37,067
When you are done, press B in the server window on the console.

44
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:42,533
R3 shrinks the window to a badge, and the server keeps running while you use Kefir

45
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:44,533
Hub.

46
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:50,067
The server also stops by itself when the console loses the network or gets a new IP

47
00:02:50,067 --> 00:02:52,067
address.

48
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:54,667
Start it again; the address may change.

49
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:56,667
Now FTP.

50
00:02:56,667 --> 00:02:59,733
Open Tools, Settings, Network and turn on FTP.

51
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:05,200
The server runs while Kefir Hub is open, and starts with it until you turn it off.

52
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:10,600
To require a login, open "FTP settings", set Username and Password, then turn off

53
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,600
"Anonymous (no login)".

54
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:17,933
In an FTP program such as FileZilla, connect to the console's IP address on port

55
00:03:17,933 --> 00:03:19,933
5000.

56
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:23,800
With the default settings any user name and password work.

57
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:29,333
At the top level of the server you see the microSD card and a folder named install.

58
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:31,333
Copy a game file into install.

59
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:36,000
The console shows "FTP Install" and installs the file while it copies.

60
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,333
There is no percentage: the FTP program does not tell the console the file size.

61
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:46,733
You see how many files are installed, how much is written, and the average speed.

62
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:51,800
To cancel, press X on the console, choose "Cancel installation" and confirm.

63
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:53,800
B does nothing here.

64
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:59,333
Files still queued in the FTP program keep coming, so stop the queue in the program

65
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:01,333
too.

66
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:06,733
Careful: a game file copied to the top level of the server is also installed, not

67
00:04:06,733 --> 00:04:08,733
saved.

68
00:04:08,733 --> 00:04:12,933
To keep a game on the card as a file, copy it into a subfolder.

69
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:17,733
Over FTP you can also copy any other files to and from the microSD card.

70
00:04:17,733 --> 00:04:21,200
The console's system memory is not visible over FTP.

71
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:25,733
Ownfoil is a game library server that you run on your own PC or NAS.

72
00:04:25,733 --> 00:04:28,867
On the Tools tab press plus and choose Ownfoil.

73
00:04:28,867 --> 00:04:31,000
Choose "Discover local servers".

74
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,933
A server that was found but is not saved yet is tagged New.

75
00:04:34,933 --> 00:04:36,933
Select it.

76
00:04:36,933 --> 00:04:40,800
Kefir Hub tells you whether the shop is public or private.

77
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,933
Yes opens the form where you can enter a login.

78
00:04:43,933 --> 00:04:47,200
No saves the server without a login and connects.

79
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:51,200
If the server is not found, press X and choose "Add server".

80
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:56,800
Enter a name and the local address with its port, for example 192.168.1.10:8465, and

81
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,800
choose Save.

82
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:03,467
The catalog opens on New games: games that are not on the console yet.

83
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:06,667
Y switches to Updates, DLC, All games or Search.

84
00:05:06,667 --> 00:05:08,667
Pick a game and press A.

85
00:05:08,667 --> 00:05:14,133
In the panel, choose the version and tick the DLC you want under "Add-on content".

86
00:05:14,133 --> 00:05:16,400
The last entry starts the install.

87
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:21,600
It is called Install, Update or Downgrade, depending on the version you chose.

88
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:25,133
A progress window shows the download and the install.

89
00:05:25,133 --> 00:05:27,733
Finally, you can share a single folder.

90
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:32,267
In the File Browser highlight a folder, press plus and choose Mount.

91
00:05:32,267 --> 00:05:34,267
Then pick MTP, FTP or HTTP.

92
00:05:34,267 --> 00:05:39,667
Mounting does not hide the rest of the card: the web page and FTP can still reach

93
00:05:39,667 --> 00:05:41,667
every folder.

94
00:05:41,667 --> 00:05:45,000
To stop sharing, choose Unmount in the same panel.

95
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,400
You can also install from a network share over SMB, NFS or WebDAV.

96
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:55,000
For that and more, read the Install over the network and Share files with a PC pages

97
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
in the documentation.
